summary:
- topic: Student Representative Recognition
  text: The board and public dedicated a significant portion of the meeting to honoring
    departing student representative Elliot Wertheimer for his dedicated and insightful
    service during his term.
- topic: Personnel
  text: The board unanimously approved several personnel elections, including the
    hiring of Abigail Chen as the new district Finance Director. Several resignations
    were also noted.
- topic: FY2026 Budget Referendum
  text: The Superintendent reminded the public about the June 10th school budget referendum
    for the 2025-2026 school year and encouraged community members to vote.
- topic: Athletics Funding Clarification
  text: It was clarified that funding for athletic complex improvements is not part
    of the upcoming June 10th budget vote and will be addressed separately at a later
    date.
- topic: Public Comment
  text: The South Portland Teachers Association (SPTA) president urged the public
    to support the budget. Other speakers expressed regret over the resignation of
    two teachers from Dyer Elementary School.
- topic: Student Leadership
  text: The board congratulated Angela Kabisa on her re-election as a student representative
    for a third year and welcomed incoming representative Alex Davison.
- topic: Special Education
  text: In response to a public question, the Assistant Superintendent stated the
    district is in a 'fact-finding' phase regarding the multi-year transition of responsibility
    for pre-K special education services from Child Development Services (CDS) to
    the district.
- topic: Executive Session
  text: The board voted to enter an executive session, after which they returned to
    formally adjourn the meeting.
